BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventexhibitionopenings3afocusatthedelaplaine22244-20261107@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261106T172124Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261108
SUMMARY:Exhibition Openings: FOCUS at The Delaplaine
DESCRIPTION:Exhibition Openings: FOCUS at The Delaplaine Saturday\, November 7 • 3–5 pm FREE View exhibitions and meet the artists! These exhibitions are opening on Saturday\, November 7 and can be viewed starting at 9 am. Beat the crowds and visit us earlier in the day! Nov 7–29 National Juried Photography Exhibition Part of FOCUS: A Celebration of Photography\, the NJPE takes place every other year in November. The exhibition features selected photographs by regional and national artists. ABOUT THE JUROR: E. Brady Robinson is a Baltimore-based photographer and creative director known for her vibrant and eclectic mix of fine art photography\, cultural documentation\, and portraits of creatives. Her work has been featured in solo and group exhibitions in the US and internationally\, and her photographs are held in the permanent collections of the Orlando Museum of Art and the Spanish Cultural Center in Santo Domingo\, Dominican Republic. Robinson teaches photography and senior seminar at Georgetown University and is a contributing photographer for BmoreArt and Baltimore Beat. Nov 7–29 Mark Seaver Beauty Through Thin Ice Photography Seaver’s photography uses ice and its properties as a filter through which to photograph. The result is the refraction of light\, which distorts and abstracts the world seen through it. Nov 7–29 Christophe Casamassima The Dirty Window Photography The Dirty Window is a phantasmagoric cycle of photography that aligns with the four stages of sleep. Casamassima uses photography to explore how repetition reveals difference and where latent images surface to consciousness before dissolving again. Nov 7–29 Kevin Stivers Elsewhere Photography Elsewhere exists between places\, neither here nor there. The work in Stiver’s exhibition explores themes of human connection and disconnect and feelings of belonging and misplacement\, shrouded in a surreal atmosphere.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/exhibition-openings%3a-focus-at-the-delaplaine/22244/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventfacetedseminarseries7chandsculpted3atheart26evolutionofengraving26237-20261107@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261106T172124Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261108
SUMMARY:FACETED Seminar Series | Hand Sculpted: The Art & Evolution of Engraving
DESCRIPTION:Join the InBloom team on Saturday\, November 7th at 3PM in their Downtown Frederick gallery for the next talk in the FACETED seminar series—Hand Sculpted: The Art & Evolution of Engraving. A hand-engraved line isn’t simply applied to jewelry—it deliberately transforms the metal. For centuries\, engravers have cut controlled lines into metal to preserve names\, create intricate patterns\, and bring surfaces and stories to life through texture\, light\, and shadow. It’s a beautiful expression of InBloom Jewelry’ philosophy: artistry in service to love. Whether a meaningful date inside a band\, a name rendered in script\, or a hand-cut design inspired by a personal story\, hand engraving makes jewelry deeply personal and enduring—meticulously carved by a person\, for a person (or by the InBloom goldsmiths\, for you). This seminar will include a fascinating discussion on the history and evolution of hand engraving and a live demonstration of this centuries-old art form. Free to all\, RSVPs encouraged.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/faceted-seminar-series-%7c-hand-sculpted%3a-the-art-%26-evolution-of-engraving/26237/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventfamilyseries3ahandmadepuppetdreams3afamiliesvoli26101-20261107@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261106T172124Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261108
SUMMARY:FAMILY Series: Handmade Puppet Dreams: Families Vol I
DESCRIPTION:Gather the family for this art-rageous collection of creative films from Volume I of Heather Henson’s Handmade Puppet Dreams film series. Challenge a Mountain Goat\, visit Old Mother Hubbard\, have a Graveyard Jamboree\, and so much more in this special collection perfect for all ages of fun-loving folks. Created during the pandemic using limited resources and boundless creativity\, these family-friendly films invite audiences of all ages (5 to 95 and above) to slow down and savor beautifully told stories made entirely by hand. From whimsical creatures to heartfelt adventures\, each short film in the Volume I collection transports viewers into visually stunning miniature worlds. This unique cinematic experience blends puppetry\, art\, and storytelling to spark curiosity and wonder in kids and adults alike. Perfect for families\, educators\, and anyone young at heart. This show is part of the Family Series\, providing affordable and inclusive programming for children and their families. The Weinberg Center\, located in the heart of Downtown Frederick\, MD\, offers a historic backdrop and timeless atmosphere for a memorable live entertainment experience for all ages. Sponsored by: Leidos Biomedical Research
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/family-series%3a-handmade-puppet-dreams%3a-families-vol-i/26101/
END:VEVENT
